id: pm-i03k
title: "presets commands redeclared host-owned --json global, failing registration on pm-cli 2026.7.27"
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 ships GH-719: the host rejects any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global flag. The presets package declared { long: \"--json\" } in a shared JSON_FLAG constant spread across presets list, presets show, presets diff, presets export, presets validate, and the bare presets command. Every one of these commands failed to register against a real pm host. The existing test suite used the SDK testing harness but had no suite-wide guard asserting the host-owned flag invariant. Fix: removed the --json flag from the JSON_FLAG constant (now empty), and changed the two handler reads of readBooleanOption(options, 'json') to ctx.global?.json === true. The --json flag still works because it is host-owned — pm accepts it and renders JSON output; the extension just must not redeclare it. Also fixed the audit:prod script which used plain 'npm audit --omit=dev' instead of the 'env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts' form required by project-scoped installs. Removed the last 'as any' cast in registry.test.ts. Added a suite-wide guard test asserting no registered command redeclares any of the nine host-owned globals. Bumped pm-cli to 2026.7.27."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T05:03:56.699Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:24:21.171Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:24:21.171Z"
author: pi-agent
release: 2026.7.27
resolution: "Presets commands re-register under pm-cli 2026.7.27 after dropping the shadowing --json declaration. Attributed to release 2026.7.27, verified by containment: git merge-base --is-ancestor dcca13e v2026.07.27 succeeds, and the tag in fact points directly at that fix commit. An earlier revision of this record claimed the release was still pending and left the item deliberately unattributed; that was based on a stale local tag set and is superseded."
expected_result: "Presets commands register successfully on pm-cli 2026.7.27, with the changelog entry under the 2026.7.27 heading that actually carried the fix."
actual_result: "Before the fix, redeclaring the host-owned --json global aborted registration at that command and dropped every later sibling, while --help still exited 0 with a misleading arity error (upstream pm-cli#772). A first closeout attempt then left the item unattributed, which incorrectly produced an Unreleased section for work that had in fact shipped."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T05:04:04.241Z",pi-agent,"Verified: activation probe prints failed=[] against the real pm host engine. npm test: 47/47 pass including the new suite-wide guard test asserting no command redeclares any host-owned global. release:check green end to end (typecheck, build, test, audit:prod, pack:dry-run, changelog:check). The --json flag is read from ctx.global.json in the presets diff and presets --diff handlers. All usage examples mentioning --json remain valid since --json still works as a host-owned global."
  "2026-07-27T23:09:37.575Z",claude-code,"Correction: this item was briefly closed with no release attribution on the belief that no v2026.07.27 tag existed. That reading came from STALE LOCAL TAGS. After git fetch --tags --force the tag is present and git merge-base --is-ancestor confirms the fix commit dcca13e is contained in v2026.07.27 -- the tag in fact points directly at it. Attributed to 2026.7.27 accordingly, so the entry sits with its siblings from the same release window instead of in Unreleased."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the fix stopping presets commands from redeclaring the host-owned --json global merged as PR #32 and shipped in release 2026.7.27, whose tag points directly at that commit."
body: ""
